{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-222059",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-{x}^{2}-18x+4 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+18x)+4 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 9x+{9}^{2}-{9}^{2})+4 \\\\  & =-((x+9)^{2}-81)+4 \\\\  & =-(x+9)^{2}+81+4 \\\\  & =-(x+9)^{2}+85\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=-(x+9)^{2}+85\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=-(y+9)^{2}+85\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-(y+9)^{2}+85 \\\\ x-85 & =-(y+9)^{2} \\\\ 85-x & =(y+9)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{85-x} & =y+9 \\\\ \\sqrt{85-x}-9 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge -9$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge -9.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{85-x}-9\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
